  "base_expansion": "Base 'Davis' expanded to standard composition: Davis minimal medium (Davis & Mingioli 1950): K2HPO4/KH2PO4, (NH4)2SO4, Na-citrate, MgSO4 + glucose.",
  "verification_evidence": "Overnight cultures of resistant and sensitive cells for each experiment were grown from single colonies and then incubated in sterile Davis Minimal Media with 1,000 g/ml glucose liquid media overnight at 30 C while rotating at 240 rpm. (the '1,000 g/ml' is a typographical error for 1,000 ug/ml = 1 g/L; agar plates used 2,000 ug/ml). The Sigma Davis Minimal Broth base also supplies dextrose at 1.0 g/L.",
  "verification_confidence": "high",
  "base_medium": "Davis Minimal Broth (Davis formulation; Davis & Mingioli 1950), Sigma-Aldrich product 93753 / Difco-BD 275610 / HiMedia M389",
