      "final pH 7.0"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "missing_before": [],
   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "Davis Minimal Broth is a fully defined minimal medium of six salts plus dextrose; it contains NO added trace-element mix and NO vitamins (E. coli is prototrophic and grows on it), so no hidden stock solution needs expanding and nothing was genuinely missing. The target's current_components already correctly decompose the salts into ions (K, Pi, NH4, SO4, citrate, Mg, Na) plus glucose/O2/H2O/H+; this record adds the compound-level recipe with concentrations. Paper is not anaerobic despite 'facultative' organism label: cultures are shaken (240 rpm) and stirred bioreactors, i.e. aerobic. Glucose "
  },
